  "post": {
   "title": "ChatGPT ads can find you by email and phone number: here's how it works",
   "tiktok_caption": "Brands can upload email and phone lists, and ChatGPT matches them to users for ads. Even with personalization off, your current chat can still pick the ad. OpenAI says advertisers never see your chats. #AI #ChatGPT #OpenAI #Privacy #AInews #FredsDesk",
   "yt_caption": "404 Media looked at how ChatGPT ads are targeted. Advertisers can upload lists of emails and phone numbers that OpenAI matches to ChatGPT users (about 25,000 matches minimum, per OpenAI). Turning ad personalization off still allows ads based on your current chat. Plus and higher plans and Temporary Chats show no ads. Follow FredsDesk for daily AI",
   "pinned_comment": "Ads appear only on the Free and Go plans; Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise and Edu are ad-free, and OpenAI says Temporary Chats show no ads. OpenAI says advertisers do not get your chats or personal details, and that being on a list does not by itself mean you get an ad. The 25,000 figure is OpenAI's minimum audience size as reported by Gadget Review, Gizmodo and MobileSyrup. Sources: 404 Media, Gizmodo, Gadget Review, MobileSyrup, OpenAI Help Center.",
   "hashtags": [
    "#AI",
    "#ChatGPT",
